    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Use the dot diagram to explain why the sum of the first $n$ odd positive integers is $n^2$.\n$$1+3+5+\\cdots+(2n-1)=n^2$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q4-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 12, p12-q4-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\foreach \\x in {0,...,6}{\n  \\foreach \\y in {0,...,6}{\n    \\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\\layerparity}{mod(max(\\x,\\y),2)}\n    \\ifnum\\layerparity=0\n      \\fill[black] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=0.9mm];\n    \\else\n      \\draw[black,line width=0.4pt,fill=white] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=1.05mm];\n    \\fi\n  }\n}\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
