          "sourcePage": 12,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 4, square dot array",
          "description": "Seven-by-seven square array of 49 equally spaced dots. Alternating filled and hollow L-shaped layers grow from the bottom-left filled dot.",
          "mathematics": "With integer coordinates x,y from 0 to 6, a dot is filled when max(x,y) is even and hollow otherwise. Layer k contains 2k+1 dots, so the first n layers form an n by n square.",
