    "children": [],
    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "Each successive odd number adds an L-shaped layer to the previous square. The first $n$ layers form an $n\\times n$ square containing $n^2$ dots.",
      "worked": "Starting from the bottom-left dot, each new L-shaped layer extends the square along two sides. The $k$th layer adds $k+(k-1)=2k-1$ dots. After $n$ layers, the diagram forms an $n\\times n$ square, so\n$$1+3+5+\\cdots+(2n-1)=n^2.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
